`i + 1` is not proven to be in range for `ys` here, so this access keeps its bounds check and compares against the length on every iteration: guard the sum with a test that reaches the access — `if (i >= 0 && i + 1 < toI32(ys.length))` proves both ends, and so does a loop condition `i + 1 < toI32(ys.length)` on a counter that starts at 0
